+/*
+ * The Wi-Fi firmware of the BALMUDA Phone (X01A), spoken to. The radio is a WCN3990; its firmware
+ * runs inside the modem (msm/modem/wlan_pd, which loads wlanmdsp.mbn), and once it is up it offers
+ * the service WLFW (QRTR service 69) on the modem's node. Before Linux's ath10k touches the radio
+ * it has an exchange with that service, and this file makes the first part of it by hand, in
+ * ath10k's order (ath10k_hw_power_on(), then ath10k_qmi_event_server_arrive() and what it calls):
+ *
+ *   0  the radio's five supplies on, through RPMh (power_on() below; wcn3990_power=0: not)
+ *   1  which indications we want: "firmware ready", "MSA ready", the pins' result
+ *   2  where the firmware's memory is (the fixed region, dt: qcom,wlan-msa-fixed-region of
+ *      qcom,icnss: pil_wlan_fw_region@8ba00000, 2 MB); the firmware answers with the regions it
+ *      makes of it, and TrustZone is asked to give each to the modem and the Wi-Fi VM. On this
+ *      phone TrustZone refuses every such move (-2, 0x56) and the firmware takes "MSA ready" all the
+ *      same, so a refusal is said and passed over
+ *   3  "MSA ready"
+ *   4  what the chip and the firmware are (chip, board id, firmware version)
+ *   5  the board's data file, bdwlan.bXX for that board id (fw/image of the system image), in pieces
+ *   6  a wait for "firmware ready"
+ *
+ * It stops there: no mode is asked for. It runs after the modem's step 10 (hakios.mpss.c) with
+ * boot-arg wcn3990=1, while the modem's link is up, and the modem is shut down after it as after any
+ * run of the steps. The phone is to be rebooted before the modem is started again.
+ *
+ * What the phone said (29 October): chip 0x320 of family 0x4001, no board id (bdwlan.bin is sent),
+ * firmware WLAN.HL.3.3.1-01557 of 13 October 2022; the board file is taken in 5 pieces; without the
+ * supplies no "firmware ready" in 10 s.
+ *
+ * The messages' descriptions below are written from the WLFW messages' published shape (QMI
+ * service 0x45, version 1); only the fields used here are described, and the decoder skips the rest.
+ *
+ * More boot-args: wcn3990_msa=0x..., wcn3990_msa_size=0x... (the region), wcn3990_ready=S (the wait
+ * of 6, default 15; Android waits 5.5 s), wcn3990_upto=N (1 to N only: a run that ends the phone loses its log, and this
+ * finds the step).
+ */
+#include <kern/clock.h>
+#include <kern/kalloc.h>
+#include <kern/thread.h>
+#include <libkern/libkern.h>
+#include <pexpert/pexpert.h>
